# ReconAgent Cursor Rules

> Modular structure: detailed guidelines live in `.cursor/rules/` and `.cursor/prompts/`.

## Quick Context

**Project:** ReconAgent — AI-powered bank reconciliation for small businesses  
**Language:** Python 3.13  
**Framework:** FastAPI (API) + LangGraph (orchestration) + Claude Code (LLM)  
**Architecture:** Agentic pipeline — PDF parsing → matching → Excel report generation

**Tech Stack:**
- API: FastAPI with async endpoints
- Orchestration: LangGraph StateGraph with Pydantic state models
- LLM: Claude Code (primary), DeepAgents (alternative), multi-provider LangChain
- Validation: Pydantic BaseModel
- Observability: LangSmith tracing
- Console: Rich

**Project Structure:**
```
src/
├── main.py              # FastAPI app + API endpoints
├── Graph/               # LangGraph state & node definitions
│   └── recon_graph.py
├── agent/               # Agent factory functions
│   └── recon_agent.py
└── prompts/             # System prompts & templates
    └── SYSTEM_PROMPT.md
user_files/              # Financial document storage (bills/, invoice/, PDFs)
```

